<div id="S5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Workload skewness.</span>
Users of multi-tenant LLM applications often access services in irregular patterns, causing sudden spikes when multiple users request simultaneously or when a application triggers bursts of usage. High skewness better represents realistic workloads in LLM serving scenarios <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>. The intervals between consecutive requests follow a Gamma distribution. When <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cv=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cv=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gamma distribution simplifies to an exponential distribution, indicating moderate burstiness. A <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cv&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cv&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> signifies significantly greater variability and pronounced bursts in request patterns. We compare <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span> with <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span> across various workload skewness scenarios under the S1@AGX setting with <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> adapters.
Table <a href="#S5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ 5.1. End-to-End Results on Synthetic Workloads ‣ 5. Evaluation ‣ EdgeLoRA: An Efficient Multi-Tenant LLM Serving System on Edge Devices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> demonstrates that <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span>’s throughput significantly decreases and its latency increases under high workload skewness. This degradation occurs because <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span> processes requests sequentially, causing delays when consecutive requests require different adapters. In contrast, <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span> experiences a modest reduction in throughput and increase in latency due to its enhanced capability for parallel request processing. These results indicate that <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span> maintains robust performance even under highly skewed workloads.
Specifically, when <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cv=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cv=2</annotation></semantics></math>, some interval between consecutive requests exceeds the request processing time, resulting in similar performance for both <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span> and <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span> when waiting for request in a long time.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>. </span><span id="S5.T9.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Throughput (req/s) comparison between <span id="S5.T9.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span>, <span id="S5.T9.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span> on S1@AGX(<math id="S5.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=50</annotation></semantics></math>) with different workload skewness.
</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T9.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T9.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T9.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><math id="S5.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cv</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S5.T9.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T9.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">llama.cpp</span></td>
<td id="S5.T9.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T9.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">EdgeLoRA</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T9.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
